=== 2. cgroup v2 limits are enforced, not silently no-op'd ===
  memory.max seen by the container: 67108864 (64 MiB = 67108864)
  same workload with --memory=64m : exit 137  (137 = SIGKILL from the OOM killer)
  same workload with no limit     : exit 0  (0 = the limit is what killed it)
  measured: true   enforced: true
  pids.max seen by the container: 16

=== 3. tcpdump captured the bridge, and what it saw ===
  packets captured: 12
  non-private destinations seen on the bridge: none

=== 4. a container killed mid-write leaves a recoverable state ===
  probe container started:     true
  real workspace on the host:  /tmp/tmp.l6IuY56ZQW
  shadow given to the probe:   /tmp/tmp.bUYWeSvR86
  probe told to write to:      /tmp/tmp.l6IuY56ZQW  (first, before the shadow loop)
  bytes written into shadow:   3145728 (of the 67108864 the probe was told to write, before the kill)
  partial write in the shadow: true (recorded, not gated: a completed write is a race)
  real workspace untouched:    true

